legend bottom
  PK = primary key; FK = foreign key; UK = unconditional unique key.
  * = NOT NULL, including implicit primary-key NOT NULL.
  Crow-foot counts follow FK nullability and unconditional uniqueness.
  Conditional unique indexes and deferred Owner checks are detailed in 3.4.5.
  Multiple named lines between tables represent distinct FK roles.
endlegend
